  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Human Rights Training Project 2022 - 2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Human Rights Training Project 2012 - 2026 is designed to strengthen the knowledge of human rights government institutions, academia, media and civil society organizations, while at the same time promoting cooperation between the various actors in Angola. Together, this will contribute to the overall goal of strengthening human rights culture in Angola, thus contributing to increased respect for human rights. The Project will promote the participation of women in training activities on human rights. It will also advocate on women&apos;s rights and build the capacity of the staff members of different public institutions to promote and apply the various legal instruments approved by Angola for the protection of women&apos;s rights. Through the training of the staff of the Ministry of Justice and Human Rights, this project has been supporting the design of the Angolan Action plan for people with disabilities. This action plan includes activities such as awareness-raising campaigns, education, and actions to eliminate discrimination against people with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
